🚶 PIR Motion Sensor Based Automatic Light Control System

📌 Project Overview

The PIR Motion Sensor Based Automatic Light Control System using Arduino UNO is an electronics project that automatically switches a light ON when human movement is detected and switches it OFF after a specified period without detected motion.

The project uses a PIR (Passive Infrared) sensor to detect movement, an Arduino UNO to process the sensor signal, and a relay module to control the light.

This system can be used in rooms, corridors, staircases, and other areas where automatic lighting is useful.

🎯 Objectives

- To detect human movement using a PIR sensor.
- To control a light automatically using an Arduino UNO.
- To operate a relay module using a digital output.
- To switch OFF the light automatically after a predefined delay.
- To demonstrate the application of sensors and microcontrollers in home automation.

