⚠️ Limitations

- PIR sensors detect changes in infrared radiation and may not detect stationary people reliably.
- Detection range depends on the sensor model and installation.
- Environmental conditions and sensor settings can affect detection.
- The relay's active-HIGH or active-LOW behavior must match the program.
- The basic system does not distinguish between people and other moving warm objects.

📚 Conclusion

The PIR Motion Sensor Based Automatic Light Control System demonstrates how a sensor, microcontroller, and relay can work together to automate lighting.

The PIR sensor detects movement, the Arduino UNO processes the signal, and the relay controls the light circuit. This project provides practical experience with embedded systems, digital inputs and outputs, and basic automation.

